  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Writing an expression as a sum of its partial Fraction and evaluating the Integral</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>1. Write the expression below as a sum of partial fractions.</p>
<p>\( \displaystyle {@question_expression@}=\)[[input:ans1]]+[[input:ans2]]</p>
<p> [[validation:ans1]] [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>2. Using the partial fractions above to compute the integral&nbsp;\(\displaystyle \int{@question_expression@}dx\).</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle\int{@question_expression@}dx =\)[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p style="">1. To write {@question_expression@} as a sum of its partial fractions we need to follow the steps below:</p>
<p style="">\[{@question_expression@} ={@question@}={@part_frac@}\].</p>
<p style="">Setting the numerators equal gives:</p>
<p style="">\[{@expr@}\]</p>
<p style="">Getting the coefficients A and B, we have</p>
<p style="">Let \(x={@bb@}:\quad {@expr1@} \implies {@expB@}\). </p>
<p style="">Let \(x={@-aa@}:\quad {@expr2@} \implies {@expA@}\).</p>
<p style="">The partial fractions of the integrand are then,</p>
<p style="">\[{@expr3@}\]</p>
<p style="">Evaluating the integral,</p>
<p style="">\[ \displaystyle\int {@question_expression@}dx= \displaystyle\int{@ta_1@}\,dx+&nbsp; \displaystyle\int{@ta_2@}\,dx \]</p>
<p style="">\[ \iff \displaystyle\int {@question_expression@}dx = {@int_part1@}+ {@int_part2@}+c\]<br></p>
<p style="">Therefore,</p>
<p style="">\[ \displaystyle\int {@question_expression@}dx= {@ta_3@}\]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
